{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-41198","model_call":12,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"diversity in nursing\" (+ importance benefits impact) (+ \"patient care\" \"patient outcomes\" \"health equity\" \"cultural competence\"))"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"diversity in nursing\" (+ importance benefits impact) (+ \"patient care\" \"patient outcomes\" \"health equity\" \"cultural competence\"))"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_132634546#0_321962125","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1421","rank":1,"snippet":"{ \"docid\": \"msmarco_v2.1_doc_40_132634546#0_321962125\" , \"end_char\": 1040.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Importance of Diversity in Nursing The Importance of Diversity in Nursing 1. The nursing workforce better represents the population. 2. Diversity increases comfort levels for patients. 3. Nurses benefit from diversity. 4. Diversity improves <cover>patient care. \" , \"segment\": \"The Importance of Diversity in Nursing | </cover>Fastaff Travel Nursing You are here Home Traveling Nurse Resources Travel Nursing News / Blog The Importance of Diversity in Nursing The Importance of Diversity in Nursing June 21, 2016 The need for diversity in the nursing workforce is acknowledged by professional organizations, employers like us, and our team of nurses. Most people know that diversity is important, but some might not know why. We’re here to share some of the reasons that a diverse hospital is a better hospital. 1. The nursing workforce better represents the population. The people living in the United States today are highly diverse. With all genders, ethnicities, and cultures living together, the nursing workforce should be representative of this population. The current nursing "},"time":108},"model_calls":12,"document_judgments":11,"relevance_3":4,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
